  "outro": [
   "Swelling, a pop, or a knee that gives way? Get it checked.",
   "Which one have *you* had?",
   "Send this to the teammate who just tweaked their knee."
  ],
  "grid_title": "KNEE INJURIES",
  "why": "ACL tear: plant and twist, often a pop, usually no contact. MCL sprain: a hit to the outside of the knee stretches or [tears](tˈɛɹz) the inner ligament. Meniscus tear: a hard twist rips one of the knee's rubbery cushions. Jumper's knee (patellar tendinitis): repeated jumping overloads the tendon just below the kneecap. Dislocated kneecap: it slips out of its groove, almost always to the outside. Pain, swelling or a knee that gives way after an injury: get it checked.",
